  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-5ce29935-7fff-6c4d-e1f0-25edf5350446&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;The proposed advertisement, by reason of its excessive size, detailed design and unsympathetic features would detract from the visual amenity of the building and undermine the character and appearance of the site and wider area. The proposal therefore comprises an incongruous and discordant feature that fails to preserve or enhance the character and appearance of the locality and is contrary to Policies LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character)  and LP7 (Advertisements) of the Hackney Local Plan 2033, London Plan Policy D3 (Optimising Site Capacity through the Design-led Approach), and the guidance set out Planning Practice guidance and in the Hackney Shopfront Design Guide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
